Uploads a channel's releases to an S3-compatible bucket (Backblaze B2, Cloudflare R2, AWS S3), so a CDN can serve updates with no server.

Credentials come from `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`, and optionally `AWS_SESSION_TOKEN`. Release files are uploaded before the channel's `index.json`, so devices never see a half-published release.

Usage: leptoskit codepush publish [OPTIONS] --endpoint <URL> --bucket <BUCKET>

Options:
      --store <STORE>
          The release store directory; defaults to `releases/`
          
          [default: releases]

      --channel <CHANNEL>
          The channel to publish
          
          [default: production]

      --platform <PLATFORM>
          Application platform; native releases use a platform-specific channel

      --endpoint <URL>
          The S3 API endpoint, such as `https://<account id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com` or `https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com`

      --bucket <BUCKET>
          The bucket name

      --region <REGION>
          The bucket's region; `auto` suits R2
          
          [default: auto]

      --prefix <PREFIX>
          A key prefix inside the bucket, so one bucket can hold more than the registry

      --path-style
          Addresses the bucket by path (`<endpoint>/<bucket>`) instead of by subdomain, for `MinIO` and other local servers

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
